From: gargrohin <29701609+gargrohin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:58:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] GR00T_N17 convert_v3_to_v2: opt-in --workers to write
 episode files in parallel

The v3.0 -> v2.1 downgrade cuts every episode out of the concatenated mp4s with one
ffmpeg call at a time (~0.15 s each), and writes the per-episode parquet files one
at a time; on EFS that is ~22 min for 2,500 episodes, almost all of it in ffmpeg.

--workers N (default 1 = sequential, same as before) runs those per-episode jobs
on N threads: each is an ffmpeg subprocess or a pyarrow write and writes its own
file, so the output does not depend on completion order. The first failure is
re-raised and pending jobs are cancelled.

Verified against the original script, outputs byte-identical (all files, incl.
every mp4, parquet and meta file):
- 5-task (250 episodes): --workers 32 and the default, 1005/1005 files.
- 50-task (2,500 episodes): --workers 32, 10005/10005 files; wall 22:20 -> 2:25
  (data 121 s -> 30 s, videos 19:38 -> 1:19).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
